  "$comment": "RB-094-21: every UI text that names a settings path (Settings > ...) is a link to its setting. `links` maps the text's i18n key to the place it opens (a key, a category, a section or a key prefix, crates/rbrowser/src/settings_window/target.rs); a notice of that key, or one whose text carries it (a failure's reason), links there in the status bar (crates/rbrowser/src/status/settings_links.rs), and a page or panel shows the link beside the text. `unlinked` names the texts that mean settings outside rBrowser, with why. The settings lint (scripts/lib/settings_links.py) fails on a mention in neither list. Texts of the settings window itself (settings.*, plugin.<id>.settings.*) and MCP tool descriptions (plugin.<id>.tools.*) need no entry. RB-094-27: a secret key (x-secret, api-client.secrets) is no setting of the window; a link to it opens the panel its x-panel names (the API client at Variables), and its text names that place (API client › Variables), never a settings path.",
